  "messages": [
    {
      "message_id": "94f1548f-3c89-48f1-8ad0-016f6d0c8df4",
      "role": "user",
      "text": "Case CONT_CONFLICTS. Consider six separate proposals in the same established timeline: (1) Without any changed motive, Rúna deliberately betrays Edda. (2) Rúna performs the harbour rescue at ten that evening, before her after-midnight arrival. (3) Rúna uses the rescue code to prevent that ship’s sinking. (4) Destroy the only usable boat before the otherwise unchanged planned escape. (5) An ordinary unexceptional letter crosses the sealed boundary. (6) Freyja and Sigrún’s real shared childhood memory motivates their first reunion. Assess these possibilities against our saved facts; do not choose resolutions for me. Pause after your response."
    },
    {
      "message_id": "afc587a8-fd10-4961-8f20-f20498e7950f",
      "role": "assistant",
      "text": "All six remain unaccepted proposals. Each raises a significant continuity conflict in the same established timeline; I have not selected a resolution.\n\n1. Motivation / oath: Rúna’s deliberate betrayal, with no changed motive, directly opposes her established oath to protect Edda (249f979b r1). The oath does not make betrayal physically impossible; the unchanged-motive proposal needs deliberate handling rather than silently discarding that commitment. Proposal ca37ee5a r1; open finding 336c0a14 r1.\n\n2. Chronology: the harbour rescue at ten that evening requires her there before her saved after-midnight arrival (4355d4e9 r1; arrival event 8b2e30d5 r1). Your explicit same-timeline ordering makes this a timing conflict. Proposal 69b1fceb r1; open finding 42774683 r1.\n\n3. Knowledge and causality: she learns the rescue code only after this ship sinks (e7860735 r1; knowledge 82dc2970 r1 before and da98ac0d r1 after sinking). Preventing that same sinking with the code requires knowledge she does not yet have and changes the learning dependency. Proposal fe6fa08b r1; open finding d0614c62 r1.\n\n4. Escape dependency: destroying the only usable boat removes the unchanged escape’s required resource (0accdfbe r1; sole-boat scope b6de28b4 r1). The escape cannot proceed as planned; I have not chosen failure, a replacement boat or a revised plan for you. Proposal bfef12dd r1; open finding 04d94072 r1.\n\n5. World rule: an ordinary letter crossing the sealed boundary contradicts “no letter can cross” (d148a2a0 r1). No exception has been supplied or adopted. Proposal d43f629f r1; open finding c8bed026 r1.\n\n6. Relationship history: a real shared childhood encounter would require prior shared history that conflicts with “never met before their reunion” (20ec7fd0 r1). I have not changed that history or reclassified the memory as false. If “shared” means something that does not require an earlier meeting, that meaning still needs clarification. Proposal 42cd4d30 r1; open finding 69b768af r1.\n\nFor each conflict, the available paths remain yours: reject or revise the proposal, explicitly revise the affected canon, supply an intentional explanation, or defer it. None has been chosen. Development of the conflicting material and promotion of the affected facts are held while the findings remain open; unrelated safe scope remains separate.\n\nExisting canon, protected directions and unanswered questions are preserved. The earlier floating-bridge uncertainty also remains open (c8ddb813 r1). Routine checkpoints remain on request. Paused here."
    }
  ],
